Grants and kill switch
Core's level: Permissive · Kill switch: off

Turn the kill switch on?
Everything "Revoke all" ends, and work running now in every pane of this Corbanu Terminal
stops, Claude panes included: a reply in progress is cancelled and its commands are
stopped, as when you interrupt it, and background terminals end.
Until you turn it off here: this Corbanu Terminal sends nothing to the model (each
new turn is refused with a message saying so), messages and tasks from other agents
wait, assignments and whips are paused, no grant can be issued, protected actions
after untrusted content are refused, the browser and memory writes are refused, and the
credential broker stays closed. Another Corbanu Terminal on this home takes the switch
when it next starts.
Saved in security_state.json: it holds after a restart. The level stays Permissive.
Turning it off later restarts nothing: work resumes only when someone acts.

enter confirm · esc cancel, nothing changes
